<img src="../img/event-writing-intensive-room.jpg" alt="The Study, where the morning diagnosis session is held" class="content-photo content-photo-left">

We meet at The Study, a small writing-focused workshop space near
downtown Portland — not a hotel conference room. Morning session runs in
the main room pictured here: comfortable chairs, good light, and enough
distance between seats that working out loud doesn't feel like a
performance.

Session one is diagnosis: what's actually stalled, and why. No pitching,
no critique — just naming the specific thing that's making the current
draft hard to return to.

<img src="../img/event-writing-intensive-courtyard.jpg" alt="The Study's garden courtyard, used for afternoon writing time" class="content-photo content-photo-right">

Afternoon session moves outside to the garden courtyard when weather
allows (there's a covered indoor alternative if it doesn't) for guided
writing time — long, unbroken blocks with occasional short check-ins,
not workshop-style discussion.

Bring a laptop or notebook, whichever you actually draft in. Coffee and
a light lunch are provided.
